Hello, and welcome to the {{ group.name }}!

Our group aims to develop shared understanding, use cases, requirements, and community specifications for cross-organizational AI agent identity and authorization. 

AI agents are increasingly operating across organizational boundaries with no open standard governing how they prove identity, who authorized them, or how they can be stopped if something goes wrong. This group develops open specifications for a cross-organizational agent identity registry — enabling verifiable, cryptographically signed credentials that travel with agents across trust domains, built on W3C Verifiable Credentials, Decentralized Identifiers, and post-quantum cryptography.

Note: 'ARIA' in our group name refers to the Agent Registry for Identity & Authorization protocol. It is unrelated to W3C WAI-ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications).

